Ekko Rose Theme for DeepSeek Harness

Visual reference and supplied artwork: the user's ekko-studio-custom repository,
local/themes/studio, rose presentation. Original Ekko source bytes are retained for the floral backdrop, wallpaper, rose and utility icons;
assets/ORIGIN.json lists source names, SHA-256 hashes and sizes. This package
makes no additional grant concerning likenesses, photographs or artwork.

Original project: https://github.com/EKKOLearnAI/ekko-studio
Custom source: https://github.com/cjjchina3088191870-sudo/ekko-studio-custom
Original project license is retained in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/Ekko-Studio-LICENSE.

Phosphor icons: original license retained in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/Phosphor-LICENSE.

The native DeepSeek Harness theme and plugin APIs are used as dependencies.
No DSH runtime or other skin's implementation/artwork is copied into this package.

Rose Queen portrait and polaroid: original fictional character artwork generated
with OpenAI imagegen in November 2026. The character is not based on a real person.
The floral hero backdrop was edited to use the Rose Queen signature while
preserving the existing floral composition. Retained frame and floral visual
references credit Codex-Dream-Skin, whose license is included.

Additional filled icons: Phosphor Icons (MIT) and Font Awesome Free
(screwdriver-wrench SVG; CC BY 4.0), tinted rose. Original license files
are retained in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

2026-11-04: rose-lace-trim-v1.webp and rose-ribbon-crest-v1.webp are generated original UI ornaments.

Startup video behavior, HTTP media helpers and bundled default startup clip are adapted from dsh-video-skin by Something11235 (MIT), commit 2f954a1d6ac6140880f1a58438ed746f2f7f3da4. See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/dsh-video-skin-LICENSE.
Shared skin manager code is distributed under the MIT license (integrated/LICENSE).

media/boot.webm is a VP8/Opus conversion of the same MIT-licensed startup clip credited above.
